    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "For Sale By Private Treaty In One Lot \n\nUnique opportunity to acquire 3 no derelict two bedroomed terraced homes on site extending to 0.086 acres. \nThese homes are derelict and in need of complete refurbishment and renovation. They present a great opportunity for anyone seeking a project in one of the more sought-after residential areas Cork has to offer. The location is second to none with the bustling village of Blackrock offering cafes as well as its popular weekly farmers market. \nThese properties have been vacant for over 2 years, therefore suitable for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant - SEAI Energy Upgrade Grants with potential funding of up to ?70,000 available to assist with renovation costs, subject to the relevant terms and conditions.\nThese homes have pedestrian access to the front and enjoy south facing enclosed rear gardens. The properties do not have any private parking.\nThere is a wide variety of primary and second level education facilities all close by combined with easy access to a host of sporting clubs from GAA to Rugby and Soccer to Hockey. Leisurely recreation is catered for at the 8km loop of the Blackrock greenway walking and cycling path which extends from the city to Passage west. Public transport connections are excellent with the 202 bus route outside the door and the 215 a short stroll away. Mahon Point, City Gate and access to the south city link road network are two minutes? drive from the property.\n\n?Development potential for sale in One Lot\n?3 x two bedroomed terraced homes\n?Folio Number CK30902L\n?These properties have been vacant for over 2 years, therefore suitable for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant of ?50,000- SEAI Energy Upgrade Grants with potential funding of up to ?70,000 available to assist with renovation costs, subject to the relevant terms and conditions.\n?Pedestrian access only - no parking\n?Enclosed rear garden.\n?The location is second to none with the bustling village of Blackrock on the doorstep along with the 8km loop of the Blackrock greenway walking and cycling path\n?Public transport connections are excellent with the 202 and 215 bus routes\n\nOutside \nPedestrian access and enclosed front garden \nEnclosed gardens to rear \n\nServices \nAll main services adjacent"
      },
